### Description

I was wondering why I get the following error:

``` AI_InvalidPromptError: Invalid prompt: messages must be an array of CoreMessage or UIMessage```



### Code example

After a longer debug session, I was able to figure out that ` "type": "tool-result" ` is missing in the toolResults response array

```js
const { text, steps, finishReason, toolCalls, toolResults } =
   await generateText({
   model,
   maxTokens: payload.maxTokens,
   temperature: payload.temperature,
   messages: initialMessages,
   tools: availableTools,
   maxSteps: 1,
 });

console.log(toolResults)
 ```
This is how the array looks like:
```
[
  {
    "toolCallId": "toolu_01MS2kwPbcjubBfCX9Sy6HEH",
    "toolName": "website",
    "args": {
      "url": "https://someurl.com"
    },
    "result": {
      "meta": null,
      "body": "some response"
    }
  }
]
```
But the array should look like

```
[
  {
     "type": "tool-result",
    "toolCallId": "toolu_01MS2kwPbcjubBfCX9Sy6HEH",
    "toolName": "website",
    "args": {
      "url": "https://someurl.com"
    },
    "result": {
      "meta": null,
      "body": "some response"
    }
  }
]
```


Temporarily fix:
``` 
 const newToolResults = toolResults.map((toolResult) => {
      return {
        ...toolResult,
        type: "tool-result",
      };
    });
```

### AI provider

@ai-sdk/anthropic v1.0.5

